        "original_id": "2e98168a-06f1-52d5-8c52-cd1b19bb4d22",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Hunt, Niki Lauda\n- Events: 1976 German Grand Prix, 1976 Formula One season\n- Places: Nürburgring\n- Organizations: Lauda Air, Austrian Airlines\n- Topics: racing helmets, media commentary, business careers\n\nFacts:\n- The 1976 German Grand Prix was a 14-lap race and the tenth round of the 1976 Formula One season.\n- James Hunt won the 1976 German Grand Prix.\n- Niki Lauda suffered a near-fatal crash at the 1976 German Grand Prix at the Nürburgring.\n- After retiring from racing in 1979, James Hunt became a media commentator and businessman.\n- Lauda Air was owned by Niki Lauda during much of its existence.\n- Lauda Air later became a charter airline subsidiary for the leisure operations of Austrian Airlines.",
